DEFINITIONS OF DONE (DoD) & CONTRACT MANDATE:
Every user story content generated or refined MUST include an explicit, language-agnostic "Definition of Done (DoD)" section containing:
1. Observable Entry Point & Black-Box Protocol Contracts: Specify executable commands, entrypoint binary paths, CLI flags, network protocols, wire formats (e.g. RESP, HTTP, JSON), and request/response envelopes. Do NOT prescribe internal module architectures, class hierarchies, or private function signatures (which belong strictly to the Generator engineering domain).
2. Anti-Stub & Anti-Gaming Invariant: Stubs, placeholders (`pass`, `...`, `NotImplementedError`, empty function blocks), shell error masking (`|| true`, `|| exit 0`, `set +e`), and tautological/vacuum tests (`assert True`, `assert 1 == 1`, unasserted mock counters) are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN. Every user story must be satisfied with real, verified, operational code.
3. Standard I/O & Output Formatting Invariants: Specify exact stdout/stderr output strings, error message prefixes (e.g. "Error: ..."), exit status codes (0 for success, non-zero for error), and interactive REPL prompt characters.
4. Explicit Data Representation & Number Formats: Specify number precision (integer vs float output representations), edge case boundaries, and empty input behaviors.
5. Comprehensive Scenario & Edge Case Matrix: Include input validation edge cases, boundary values, error conditions, and unexpected input handling scenarios.
6. Verification Criteria: Mandate 100% pass rate on unit, integration, and black-box E2E test suites with zero test failures. Do NOT include zero-linter-error requirements in intermediate feature stories; linting is non-blocking advisory during feature delivery.
7. Chicago-School Testing & Dependency Injection (DI) Invariant: DoD MUST mandate Chicago-school unit tests (testing observable state transitions on real domain objects, strictly forbidding mocking internal collaborators) with Dependency Injection for external boundaries (e.g. Store(clock=FakeClock()), in-memory stream buffers).
8. Black-Box E2E All-Scenario Invariant: DoD MUST mandate black-box E2E tests covering all scenarios (happy paths, boundary conditions, error exit codes, and output formatting) executed with socket readiness polling rather than static sleep delays.
9. Deterministic Time & Mock Clock Invariants: Every feature involving time, timers, dates, TTL, expiration, or wall-clock schedules MUST mandate deterministic mock clocks (e.g. Store(clock=FakeClock())) in the DoD to eliminate 1-second boundary assertion race conditions.
10. Pinned Directory & Required File Paths: If SPEC.md specifies a pinned directory layout or explicitly named required manifest/source files (e.g. pyproject.toml, Cargo.toml, package.json, Makefile, src/main.py, src/main.rs, cmd/todo/main.go), the Definition of Done MUST explicitly list EVERY ONE of those required file paths by exact name so downstream planners and generators create all required files.
11. Machine-Readable Story Contract: Include exactly one fenced `noctifab-contract` JSON block in every story. It MUST contain `story_id` and at least one `public_contracts` entry with a unique lowercase ID, interface, repository-relative allowed executable paths, and at least one declared observable expectation (`exit_codes`, `stdout_contains`, or `stderr_prefixes`). Use this exact shape:
